' oxygen_live.jdb - live code for oxygen_synth.jdb while it plays.
'
' oxygen_synth.jdb copies this example to oxygen_live.jdb (not in git) on its
' first start and runs that file again each time it is saved: the keyboard
' keeps playing, the audio does not stop, and a mistake only shows up in the
' status line (and the console). Edit it in any editor, or have Claude write
' it through the jdBasic MCP.
'
' The file runs at the top level of the running program, so it reads and
' sets its globals and calls its SUBs:
'   bpm, SOUND.BPM bpm              tempo
'   SELECT_PATCH(i)                 lead patch i of the bank (0-based)
'   SOUND.PARAM(1, "CUTOFF", 2400)  any parameter; track 1 lead, 0 bass, 2 drums
'   SOUND.MATRIX("LFO1", 1, "CUTOFF", 0.4)   a modulation slot
'   DRUM_ROW("hh", "x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.")       one drum row, one char per 16th,
'                                            repeated over the loop
'   SET_BARS(2), LOOP_PLAY(), LOOP_STOP(), CLEAR_LOOP()
'   arp_i = 3 : chord_i = 3 : APPLY_ARP()   arp and chord on the lead keys,
'                                         indexes into arp_modes$, arp_rates$,
'                                         chord_names$, scale_roots$, scale_modes$
'   SOUND.ZONESET 1, {"arp": "random", "arp_rate": "1/16T"}   the same, direct
'   lyric$ = "wi ar ro bots" : sing_on = TRUE : SING_START()   the lead keys sing
' Tracks 0-3 belong to the synth and the looper. Tracks 4-15 are free for
' patterns of your own; the program never touches them:
'   SOUND.VOICE 4, "SQUARE", 0.01, 0.1, 0.5, 0.2
'   SOUND.SEQ 4, "<c5 e5 g5 b4>*4", "VOICE"
' A FUNC or LAMBDA written here sees only what this file defines; give it
' what it needs as parameters.

' Everything below is an example; every line is a comment until you remove
' the quote in front of it.

' bpm = 118
' SOUND.BPM bpm
' DRUM_ROW("bd", "x...x...x...x...")
' DRUM_ROW("hh", "..x...x...x...x.")
' SOUND.PARAM(1, "REVERB", 0.4)
' SOUND.VOICE 4, "TRIANGLE", 0.01, 0.2, 0.4, 0.3
' SOUND.SEQ 4, "~ [e5 g5] ~ b5", "VOICE"
' SAY("live: groove 1")
